## 5. The one dispatcher command

Every mode is this one command, with `--host codex --yes --exec-subagents` baked in:

```bash
uv run {UV_RUN_FLAGS} --project "{SKILL_DIR}" -- python "{SKILL_DIR}/multi_llm.py" <mode> "<plan-path>" --host codex --yes --exec-subagents [flags…]
```

Exit codes are uniform (`0` done, `1` error, `2` nothing to do / already complete,
`3` needs a human) and the last stdout line is always `MULTI_LLM_RESULT: {…}`: read
`state`, `artifacts` and `next` from it rather than mining the transcript (on `state: partial`, name the failed models and their reasons from `progress.models`).
{NEEDS_HUMAN_RULE} Run `next` as printed, never re-typed: its plan path as printed, no flag added or dropped. Never pipe a dispatcher command through `cut`, `head` or `grep`: they chop the result line. `user_next_step` is the phase after this one, for the user to type: never run it yourself; end your report with its `command`, and each `optional_before` command, every one in its own fenced block, verbatim.

A fan-out mode outlives one shell call, so add `--detach`, then poll the command the launcher printed —
it carries `--host`, `--run-id` on an `ask` run, and `--wait` with no `--timeout` — one call per turn:
read the **exit code** (`0` finished, `2` still running, `3` needs a human, `1` unreadable), relay the
view's `progress:` line verbatim, and never sleep in one command. That wait is `progress.poll_s` (90 s) in full — codex documents no shell-command cap for it to sit under:

```bash
uv run {UV_RUN_FLAGS} --project "{SKILL_DIR}" -- python "{SKILL_DIR}/multi_llm.py" status "<plan-path>" --host codex --view run --wait
```

## 6. Examples — the argument forms, however this host invokes the skill

```text
/multi-llm plans/my-feature.md                       # {DEFAULT_MODE} (the default)
/multi-llm --full plans/my-feature.md                # the whole workflow
/multi-llm --ask "plans/my plan.md" "Is the rollback strategy sufficient?"
```

Providers and models come from the skill's own `providers.yaml` (per-repository
override via `--init`); `docs/providers.md` in the repository has the rest.
